{
  "case_id": "2009-08-861",
  "document_hash": "ab477e320078a510e893f0b7ad918bd4c87e981cfa32edbf77264531e7fb0fc6",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-861",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab477e320078a510e893f0b7ad918bd4c87e981cfa32edbf77264531e7fb0fc6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab477e320078-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:03 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Free Enterprise Fund and Beckstead and Watts (Petitioners)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-861",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab477e320078a510e893f0b7ad918bd4c87e981cfa32edbf77264531e7fb0fc6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab477e320078-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The board is unique among Federal regulatory agencies in that the President can neither appoint nor remove its members, nor does he have any ability to designate the chairman or review the work product, so he is stripped of the traditional means of control that he has over the traditional independent agencies."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-861",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab477e320078a510e893f0b7ad918bd4c87e981cfa32edbf77264531e7fb0fc6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab477e320078-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Why do you call it an independent regulatory agency?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Free Enterprise Fund and Beckstead and Watts (Petitioners)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-861",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab477e320078a510e893f0b7ad918bd4c87e981cfa32edbf77264531e7fb0fc6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab477e320078-0000-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "It cannot, for example, stop what happened to the Petitioners here. There is no mechanism in the statute, in any way, shape, or form, for the SEC to stop an inspection or investigation as it is ongoing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Free Enterprise Fund and Beckstead and Watts (Petitioners)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-861",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab477e320078a510e893f0b7ad918bd4c87e981cfa32edbf77264531e7fb0fc6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab477e320078-0000-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "That is a very serious burden on American citizens. That is something that is totally outside the SEC's control."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-861",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab477e320078a510e893f0b7ad918bd4c87e981cfa32edbf77264531e7fb0fc6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab477e320078-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Is it unconstitutional\nfor the President not to be able to appoint an inferior\nofficer?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Carvin",
      "case_id": "2009-08-861",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab477e320078a510e893f0b7ad918bd4c87e981cfa32edbf77264531e7fb0fc6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab477e320078-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One is: The SEC cannot be a department\nunder Freytag, because it is an independent agency\nindistinguishable from the Tax Court. And -- and what\nthe Freytag majority opinion said was, if you are unlike\na cabinet department because you are not subject to\npolitical oversight, then --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-861",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab477e320078a510e893f0b7ad918bd4c87e981cfa32edbf77264531e7fb0fc6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab477e320078-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: But that's -- that's the\nhistory and tradition of this board, which isn't very\nlong. But the history and tradition of boards like this\nis that their investigative powers are independent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Kagan",
      "case_id": "2009-08-861",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab477e320078a510e893f0b7ad918bd4c87e981cfa32edbf77264531e7fb0fc6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab477e320078-0001-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL KAGAN: Well, that's exactly right.\nAny sanction, any final inspection --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-861",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab477e320078a510e893f0b7ad918bd4c87e981cfa32edbf77264531e7fb0fc6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab477e320078-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm sorry, I asked you whether there were any consequences from the failure of the company to turn over documents; and is your answer that there are no consequences whatever?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2009-08-861",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab477e320078a510e893f0b7ad918bd4c87e981cfa32edbf77264531e7fb0fc6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab477e320078-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, let me give you an example. Suppose the President objects to the -- the very large salaries that the members of the board receive. What are their salaries?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-861",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab477e320078a510e893f0b7ad918bd4c87e981cfa32edbf77264531e7fb0fc6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab477e320078-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can the President pick up the phone and fire the SEC commissioners?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jeffrey A. Lamken",
      "case_id": "2009-08-861",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab477e320078a510e893f0b7ad918bd4c87e981cfa32edbf77264531e7fb0fc6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab477e320078-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The SEC has pervasive authority over every aspect of the board's operations. Board rules and sanctions have no effect, except as the SEC allows, and can be changed by the SEC at any time."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-861",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab477e320078a510e893f0b7ad918bd4c87e981cfa32edbf77264531e7fb0fc6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab477e320078-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But this isn't subject to the operations of the President, if he has to go through an independent agency. Are you encouraging the President, on an ongoing, daily basis, to instruct an independent agency what he wants done?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-861",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab477e320078a510e893f0b7ad918bd4c87e981cfa32edbf77264531e7fb0fc6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab477e320078-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So what is your position about the authority of the President? Is it more than for cause or only for cause?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2009-08-861",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "ab477e320078a510e893f0b7ad918bd4c87e981cfa32edbf77264531e7fb0fc6",
      "evidence_id": "ev-ab477e320078-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you know of any instance where that has happened?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2009-08-861",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "ab477e320078a510e893f0b7ad918bd4c87e981cfa32edbf77264531e7fb0fc6",
